WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.925
Note: This video is part of your Module 1 classroom

00:07.925 --> 00:10.800
instruction. The visit and tour of the mine,

00:10.800 --> 00:13.737
required by Part 48, is a separate,

00:13.737 --> 00:15.100
in-person step.

00:18.425 --> 00:21.875
Welcome to Clover Bottom Quarry #1 and #2.

00:21.875 --> 00:24.062
This video walks you through the site before your

00:24.062 --> 00:26.762
in-person tour, so you know where things are and

00:26.762 --> 00:29.700
how we work here. Clover Bottom is both a surface

00:29.700 --> 00:32.474
quarry and an underground mine. Underground there

00:32.474 --> 00:38.349
are two mines, Mine number one, MSHA ID 15-00112,

00:38.349 --> 00:43.887
and Mine number two, MSHA ID 15-19898.

00:43.887 --> 00:47.050
It produces crushed stone, from base and DGA to

00:47.050 --> 00:50.550
clean stone sizes. The drawing is an illustration,

00:50.550 --> 00:52.962
not a map. Your instructor will show you the real

00:52.962 --> 00:53.600
one.

00:54.718 --> 00:56.855
Every shift starts at the tag board.

00:56.855 --> 01:00.168
Clover Bottom has one tag board with three sections:

01:00.168 --> 01:03.031
in Mine number one on the left, out in the middle,

01:03.031 --> 01:04.918
and in Mine number two on the right.

01:04.918 --> 01:07.318
Tag in under the mine you're actually entering,

01:07.318 --> 01:09.480
and tag out every time you come out.

01:09.480 --> 01:12.493
With two mines on one surface, a tag in the wrong

01:12.493 --> 01:15.318
section could send rescuers to the wrong mine.

01:15.318 --> 01:18.230
Never tag for anyone else. Visitors use a separate

01:18.230 --> 01:19.068
check-in.

01:22.425 --> 01:24.550
Here's how traffic moves on this site.

01:24.550 --> 01:27.325
Haul trucks run from the surface pit and the underground

01:27.325 --> 01:29.638
mine to the plant; road trucks come through the

01:29.638 --> 01:32.837
scale. Pedestrians stay on the marked walkways,

01:32.837 --> 01:35.525
and nobody walks on a haul road. The speed limit

01:35.525 --> 01:38.375
is 15 miles per hour everywhere on site.

01:38.375 --> 01:40.713
Traffic is two-way and keeps right,

01:40.713 --> 01:42.637
and haul trucks have the right of way.

01:42.637 --> 01:45.213
In a pickup, call the haul truck on the radio before

01:45.213 --> 01:47.862
you approach it. Watch for overhead power lines

01:47.862 --> 01:50.675
on the surface and in Mine 1. Your instructor will

01:50.675 --> 01:53.713
show you the actual haul routes. Remember:

01:53.713 --> 01:55.987
make contact with an operator and get an answer

01:55.987 --> 01:58.613
back before you approach any equipment.

01:59.738 --> 02:02.550
We communicate by radio; your supervisor will give

02:02.550 --> 02:05.576
you the channels and call words. Warning signals

02:05.576 --> 02:08.988
here include the horn and backup alarms on equipment,

02:08.988 --> 02:11.251
the plant start-up horn, and the blast warning

02:11.251 --> 02:12.063
signal.

02:15.409 --> 02:18.171
The basic cycle here is drill, blast,

02:18.171 --> 02:21.983
load, haul and crush. Drilling and blasting are

02:21.983 --> 02:24.771
done by our own Allen crew, both in the surface

02:24.771 --> 02:28.058
pit and underground. In the pit, benches are about

02:28.058 --> 02:31.696
65 feet high. Underground, both mines are worked

02:31.696 --> 02:34.608
room and pillar, and the rooms are about 30 by

02:34.608 --> 02:37.371
40 feet. You'll see both for yourself on your mine

02:37.371 --> 02:40.308
tour. Never work near a highwall or with your back

02:40.308 --> 02:41.096
to one.

02:42.234 --> 02:44.334
The plant is where you'll find crushers,

02:44.334 --> 02:47.409
screens and conveyors; stay on walkways and out

02:47.409 --> 02:50.097
of guarded areas. The shop has its own rules for

02:50.097 --> 02:52.947
lockout and hot work. The scale house is where

02:52.947 --> 02:55.284
trucks are weighed before they leave the pit.

02:58.600 --> 03:00.937
Each mine has its own escapeway map.

03:00.937 --> 03:04.100
Escapeways are marked on the maps with green arrows.

03:04.100 --> 03:06.925
Underground, the primary escapeway is marked with

03:06.925 --> 03:09.562
white reflectors on the ribs, and the secondary

03:09.562 --> 03:12.562
with blue reflectors, along with reflective signs

03:12.562 --> 03:15.550
and arrows. Mine number one's map is posted in

03:15.550 --> 03:18.350
the breakroom and at the drill steel building near

03:18.350 --> 03:21.737
the Liwell plant. Mine number two's is in the breakroom

03:21.737 --> 03:22.812
and at the portal.

03:23.938 --> 03:26.938
In an emergency, go to a gathering point:

03:26.938 --> 03:29.738
the tag board, which is signed Emergency Assembly

03:29.738 --> 03:32.975
Area 1, the old mine entrance, or behind the mine

03:32.975 --> 03:35.563
where the haul road to the asphalt plant is.

03:36.726 --> 03:40.163
For a serious injury or fire, call 911.

03:40.163 --> 03:43.776
Jackson County E911 dispatches all three.

03:43.776 --> 03:49.301
Tell them: Clover Bottom Quarry, 12420 US-421 N,

03:49.301 --> 03:51.788
McKee, and where the injured person is:

03:51.788 --> 03:55.663
underground, pit, plant, scale or shop.

03:55.663 --> 03:57.876
Then call the mine office so someone meets the

03:57.876 --> 04:01.063
ambulance at the gate. Nearby hospitals are AdventHealth

04:01.063 --> 04:04.126
Manchester, Saint Joseph Berea, Baptist Health

04:04.126 --> 04:07.063
Richmond. Mine rescue comes from the Kentucky Division

04:07.063 --> 04:09.863
of Mine Safety's Crestwood and Hazard mine rescue

04:09.863 --> 04:10.888
stations.

04:12.022 --> 04:14.472
Your in-person mine tour is the next,

04:14.472 --> 04:16.935
separate step. Ask questions about anything you

04:16.935 --> 04:17.672
see.

04:18.784 --> 04:21.946
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

04:21.946 --> 04:23.446
override this video.
